---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site, contact } from "@/data/siteConfig";
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="Read, learn, and share what is here — but do not attack the site, and do not treat anything written here as professional advice."
>
  <p>
    These terms are short on purpose. By using this site you accept them. If you do not
    accept them, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>“This site”, “the site”</strong> — the website at {site.url}, including every page
      and file served from it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“I”, “me”, “the owner”</strong> — {site.fullName}, who runs this site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Author”</strong> — the author of any written work published on this site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“You”, “visitor”, “user”</strong> — anyone who uses the site or anything on it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Content”</strong> — everything published on this site: articles, blog posts,
      books and e-books, notes, project and experience entries, images, and downloads.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Written works”</strong> — the written content on this site, covered by the
      <a href="/works-license-v1">Works License - V1</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Works License - V1”</strong> — the license published at
      <a href="/works-license-v1">{site.url}/works-license-v1</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What you may do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Read everything here freely. “Freely” means freedom, not free of cost: some things on
      this site are paid, and the price of each is stated explicitly on its own page.
    </li>
    <li>Share links to any page.</li>
    <li>
      Copy and reuse the written works under the Works License - V1, which is the license
      that applies to them unless a work explicitly states otherwise — including its
      attribution and no-modification conditions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What you may not do</h2>
  <p>The site runs for visitors, not for exploitation. You may not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      access, probe, scan, or attempt to break into any part of the site or its host that you
      are not authorised to access;
    </li>
    <li>
      hack, exploit, inject anything into, or attempt to bypass the security or access
      controls of the site;
    </li>
    <li>
      attack, flood, overload, or otherwise disrupt the site (denial of service, brute force,
      or similar);
    </li>
    <li>upload or transmit malware, or use the site to distribute it;</li>
    <li>
      run automated requests at a volume that degrades the site or blocks other visitors;
    </li>
    <li>impersonate the owner or anyone else;</li>
    <li>use the site to break any law or to harm another person;</li>
    <li>
      use anything you learn here about security against a system you do not own or have
      written permission to test.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Educational purpose only — not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on this site — cybersecurity, Islamic knowledge, business, and personal
    writing — is general educational material. It is not financial, investment, legal,
    medical, or professional advice, and it is not a consultation. Reading it creates no
    advisor, client, or professional relationship of any kind.
  </p>
  <p>
    For religious rulings, consult a qualified scholar. For financial, medical, or legal
    decisions, consult a qualified professional. Verify anything technical before relying on
    it; such content can become outdated quickly.
  </p>

  <h2>5. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site and its contents are provided as they are. No guarantee is made that they are
    accurate, complete, current, or always available. Links to other sites are not
    endorsements, and those sites are outside my control.
  </p>

  <h2>6. You are responsible for your own actions</h2>
  <p>
    You use this site, and anything you take from it, entirely at your own risk. The owner of
    this site and the author of any writing on it are not responsible or liable for any
    action you take based on the content, or for any loss, damage, or legal consequence that
    follows from it. That responsibility belongs to you alone.
  </p>

  <h2>7. No harassment, attacks, or claims</h2>
  <p>
    You agree not to harass, threaten, defame, or attack the author — in person, online, or
    technically — and not to bring any claim or legal action against the author regarding the
    contents of this site. Disagreement is welcome and can be raised directly; abuse is not.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in this section removes a right that the law does not allow to be removed.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated. The date at the top of this page shows the current version.
    Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
